Oh, yeah, just doing it that way with skill core the scope of all enemies would count as resolving the action on each - that was my bad.
To get that to work properly, you'll need to either program the skill using Yanfly's Action Sequences, or use Auto Passive States (which also requires Buffs & States).
The latter is a bit simpler - you'd make a state that's granted as a passive state by the skill. You'll also need a game switch - I'll use ID 69, you change it to whatever.
Then you give the state:
Code:
<Custom Turn Start Effect>
$gameSwitches.setValue(69, false);
</Custom Turn Start Effect>
And you change the skill notetag to read:
Code:
<Post-Damage Eval>
if (!$gameSwitches.value(69))
{
    $gameParty.aliveMembers().forEach(actor =>
    {
        actor.gainHp(v[42]);
        actor.startDamagePopup();
    });
    $gameSwitches.setValue(69, true);
}
</Post-Damage Eval>
